A||||3||making it better||rebuilding motor; going from 2.8L to 3.1L||||1||
Z||000000||making it better||12-01-2000||06:30 PM||||I own a 87GT 2.8L.  the clutch went so I dropped the motor and decided to rebuild it.  The engine block and heads are being cleaned right now.  I want to make it a 3.1L.  I have been told two different things, one is you only have to change crank and pistons and the other is you have to bore it out. Can someone tell me which is right.  If anyone else has anyother ideas on getting more horsepower I would appreciate them.  I am only a novice mechanic and don't want to do anything that is complicated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-01-2000||06:45 PM||||i have a 3.1, but i got it out of a Z24 complete. I think it does require a diff crank. I dont think its a rebore, just changes stroke to get the extra displacement.the kit they sell is called a 'stroker kit'||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||12-01-2000||07:00 PM||||The 3.1 only requires a stroker kit. Not a rebore. The 3.2 is a bored out and stroked 2.8. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||12-01-2000||07:25 PM||||2.8 to 3.1  -need crank, pistons and a neutral balance flywheel(88 2.8s were already neutral)||||reg||1
